# xcb-proto — libxcb's protocol descriptions + its C-header *generator*. That
# generator (xcbgen) is a BUILD-TIME-ONLY python tool run HOST-side to emit C;
# nothing python ends up on the disc (xcb-proto is a BDEPEND of libxcb, so it
# builds for CBUILD and never enters the target rootfs — "Python stays out" is
# about the RUNTIME image, not the build host). Our global USE="-*" strips all
# PYTHON_TARGETS, which violates xcb-proto's REQUIRED_USE (any-of
# python_targets_*); enable the builder's python — the pinned stage3
# (TOOLCHAIN_EPOCH) defaults to python3_14 (profiles/base/make.defaults). Both
# the -r1 (PYTHON_TARGETS) and -single (PYTHON_SINGLE_TARGET) forms are set so
# this holds whichever python eclass xcb-proto/libxcb use; unmatched USE_EXPAND
# flags are harmlessly ignored.
x11-base/xcb-proto python_targets_python3_14 python_single_target_python3_14
